QuestGuidance.Register("en",71,{
[2241]="7003031A\n1\tTalk to Reeve Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tReeve Ingbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. You have come to Eaworth to learn what its people know of the Uruks you are seeking.\n2\tTalk to Léowulf and attend the meagre feast\tIngbert's steward Léowulf is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Reeve Ingbert has reluctantly agreed to provide a feast for you and your companions, the very minimum amount of hospitality required by his customs.\n3\tTalk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tReeve Ingbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. You have feasted with Ingbert and now he is waiting to speak with you.\n4\tTalk to Corudan in Eaworth\tCorudan is in Eaworth. You have spoken with Ingbert and learned that the Uruks passed north of Eaworth, followed by the Third Marshal of the Riddermark.\n",
[2242]="70030326\n1\tTalk to Sidgar\030Talk to Pendhelm\tHorn is looking for Nona in Eaworth. Corudan thinks you should ask around to see if anyone has seen Nona, and if you cannot find her, you should look for Horn.\n2\tTalk to Corudan in Eaworth\tCorudan is in Eaworth. Horn is convinced that Nona has left your group for some reason, and that she will return.\n",
[2243]="7001AC19\n1\tTalk to Issuriel at Cerin Amroth\tIssuriel of Lothlórien can be found on the high flet atop Cerin Amroth. Haldir has told you of the preparations being made for the departure of the Golden Host into Mirkwood and desired that you speak with Issuriel, an Elf being considered to lead the Malledhrim. She had questions to ask of you concerning the capture of Mazog.\n2\tTalk to Issuriel and recount the story of your escape from Rushdurinul\tIssuriel is on the high flet atop Cerin Amroth, in Lothlórien. Issuriel wishes to hear the account of your escape from Rushdurinul with the captive Mazog, as the other Elves present were reluctant to tell her the rest of the story.\n3\tTalk to Issuriel at Cerin Amroth\tIssuriel is on the high flet atop Cerin Amroth, in Lothlórien. You have recounted the rest of the tale concerning your escape from Rushdurinul with Mazog, and Issuriel has heard something to cause her concern.\n",
[2244]="700479F9\n1\tFind Daervunn at the northern edge of the Camp of the Host\tDaervunn is at the northern edge of the Camp of the Host, where the road leaves the encampment and passes into Dagorlad. Aragorn has asked you to see if Daervunn has readied the men to march.\n2\tTalk to Daervunn at the northern edge of the Camp of the Host\030Talk to Pippin Took at the northern edge of the Camp of the Host\tDaervunn and Pippin are at the edge of the Camp of the Host, where the northward road leads into Dagorlad.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Host\tAragorn is on the rise in the middle of the Camp of the Host. Daervunn reported that the men are ready to march.\n4\tTalk to Mithrandir at the Camp of the Host\tMithrandir is at the Camp of the Host on the border of Dagorlad. Something has worried Mithrandir and he wishes to speak to you about it.\n5\tTalk to Mithrandir and experience 'Interlude: No Other Way' or read the shortened account instead\tMithrandir is at the Camp of the Host on the border of Dagorlad. Mithrandir is worried about what might have befallen Frodo and Sam since they parted ways with Faramir in Ithilien.\n6\tTalk to Mithrandir at the Camp of the Host\tMithrandir is at the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad.\n7\tTalk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Host\tAragorn is on the rise in the middle of the Camp of the Host.\n",
[2245]="7000018E\n1\tTalk to Laerdan\tLaerdan is at Gath Forthnír. Golodir, crushed by his daughter's death, told you to leave him be and to go speak with the Elf Laerdan. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tBring Golodir's gear to Laerdan\030Find Prakhum, the emissary of Goblin-town, and recover Golodir's sword from him\030Find Karstíona, the emissary of the Trév Duvárdain, and recover Golodir's mail shirt from her\030Find Laugi Goldentongue, the emissary of the Dourhands, and recover Golodir's shield from him\tGolodir's gear was given to emissaries from the goblins, dwarves and nomads of Angmar. These emissaries can be found in the spires surrounding Barad Gúlaran to the south of Gath Forthnír. As a first step in his plan to renew Golodir's spirit, Laerdan has asked you to retrieve the Ranger's weapons and gear from the emissaries within the towers of Barad Gúlaran. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n",
[2246]="700301C5\n1\tComplete all quests in Langhold, in the Wold\030Learn how to participate in mounted combat at the Tourney Field in Harwick\tIn order to obtain war-steeds for yourself and your companions, you will need to accomplish two things: complete the preparations for and defence of Langhold, and learn about mounted combat in Harwick. The defence of Langhold involves a chain of ten quests that begins with a quest bestowed by Dala called 'The Wold.' If Dala has no more quests for you, search around Langhold for other quest-givers. You can learn about mounted combat at the Tourney Field in Harwick.\n2\tTalk to Nona\030Talk to Horn\030Talk to Corudan\tYour companions have obtained war-steeds of their own, and are waiting to speak with you in Harwick, by the tourney ground near the stables.\n3\tTalk to Enstan\tEnstan is by the south-east exit of Harwick, in the Wold. Your companions have war-steeds of their own and now you have heard that Enstan wants your help with something urgent.\n",
[2247]="700479FB\n1\tTalk to Lothrandir south of the rise in the Camp of the Host\tLothrandir is south of Aragorn's position on the rise in the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad. Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.\n2\tTalk to Lothrandir south of the rise in the Camp of the Host\tLothrandir is south of Aragorn's position on the rise in the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad. Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.\n3\tTalk to Radanir to the south-east of Lothrandir's position in the Camp of the Host\tRadanir is south-east of Lothrandir's position in the Camp of the Host on the border of Dagorlad. Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.\n4\tTalk to Radanir to the south-east of Lothrandir's position in the Camp of the Host\tRadanir is south-east of Lothrandir's position in the Camp of the Host on the border of Dagorlad. Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.\n5\tTalk to Corunir east of Radanir's position in the Camp of the Host\tCorunir is east of Radanir's position in the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad. Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.\n6\tTalk to Corunir east of Radanir's position in the Camp of the Host\tCorunir is east of Radanir's position in the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad. Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.\n7\tTalk to Calenglad north of Corunir's position in the Camp of the Host\tCalenglad is north of Corunir's position in the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad. Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.\n8\tTalk to Calenglad north of Corunir's position in the Camp of the Host\tCalenglad is north of Corunir's position in the Camp of the Host, on the border of Dagorlad. Aragorn wanted you to express to some of his kinsmen how grateful he is for the sacrifices they have made, and will make, in his service.\n9\tTalk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Host\tAragorn is on the rise in the middle of the Camp of the Host.\n10\tTalk to Aragorn in the Camp of the Host\tAragorn is on the rise in the middle of the Camp of the Host.\n",
[2248]="7000018F\n1\tBring Golodir's equipment to Daervunn\tDaervunn is at Esteldín in the North Downs, far to the south and west of Angmar. Laerdan instructed you to take Golodir's equipment to the Ranger Daervunn to be repaired.\n2\tBring the sword and shield to Toram\tToram is in Esteldín. Daervunn felt he could repair Golodir's shirt, but the sword and shield were beyond his ability. He asked you to speak to Toram in Esteldín to have those items repaired.\n3\tTalk to Toram\tReclaim Golodir's sword and shield from Toram in Esteldín. Daervunn asked you to take Golodir's sword and shield to Toram, an armour-smith in Esteldín, for repair.\n4\tBring the sword and shield to Daervunn\tDaervunn is at Esteldín. You should return to Daervunn to collect Golodir's shirt and to see if he has any thoughts on how to repair Golodir's sword.\n",
[2249]="700301CA\n1\tTalk to Goldlac at the entrance to Floodwend\tFloodwend is south-east of Harwick, along the road. You have agreed to ride to the defence of Floodwend.\n2\tDefeat Easterlings in the Wold (total: 5)\030Collect salvaged belongings (total: 5)\tEasterlings are crossing into the Wold south of the rapids of Sarn Gebir, and you need to defeat them and gather their scattered belongings.\n3\tBring salvaged belongings to Goldlac at the entrance to Floodwend\tGoldlac is at the entrance to Floodwend, in the Wold. You have defeated Easterlings and collected their salvaged supplies, and should return now to Goldlac.\n4\tTalk to Corudan by the entrance to Floodwend\tCorudan is by the entrance to Floodwend. Corudan wants to speak with you about the bow that Elfsige took from a dead Orc near Floodwend.\n",
[2250]="700479FC\n1\tDefeat foes in the Noman-lands (total: 6)\tAragorn asked you to defeat a number of threatening foes in the Noman-lands.\n2\tAfter you defeated threatening foes in the Noman-lands, Aragorn wanted you to meet up with Langlas in the ruin of Haerondir, north-east of the Camp of the Host.\t\n3\tFind Dûm Boha in the Noman-lands, east of Haerondir\030Find the road to Dol Acharn in Dagorlad, north-east of Haerondir\030Find Ondoher's Folly in Dagorlad, north of Haerondir\030Defeat foes in the Noman-lands and Dagorlad (total: 14)\tLanglas asked you to find locations in the Wastes where enemies might threaten the Host of the West, and to defeat any foes you find. The sites of concern to him are: Dûm Boha, east of Haerondir, in the Noman-lands. Dol Acharn, north-east of Haerondir, on the field of Dagorlad Ondoher's Folly, north of Haerondir, on the field of Dagorlad After you have accomplished these tasks, Langlas asked you to meet with Aragorn before the Black Gate.\n4\tFind Aragorn on the northern side of the Slag-hills outside the Black Gate\tAragorn and the Host of the West planned to meet you at the base of the Slag Hills outside the Black Gate once you scouted the Wastes.\n5\tTalk to Aragorn at the base of the slag-hill outside the Black Gate\tAragorn and the Host of the West planned to meet you at the base of the Slag-hills outside the Black Gate once you scouted the Wastes.\n6\tClimb atop the slag-hill and look south to the Black Gate\tAragorn asked you to climb to the top of the slag-hill and look south to the Black Gate of Mordor.\n7\tTalk to Aragorn at the base of the slag-hill outside the Black Gate\tAragorn is at the base of the slag-hill before the Black Gate.\n",
[2251]="700001E7\n1\tBring Golodir's gear to Elrond\tElrond is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws. Daervunn suggested you take Golodir's sword to Elrond of Rivendell to be reforged.\n2\tBring Golodir's gear to Hemeldir\tHemeldir can be found near Rivendell's forges. Elrond instructed you to take Golodir's sword to his chief smith, Hemeldir, to be reforged.\n3\tCollect Golodir's sword from Hemeldir\tHemeldir can be found near Rivendell's forges. You should check with Hemeldir to learn if he has finished reforging Golodir's sword.\n4\tBring Golodir's sword to Elrond\tElrond is in Rivendell. Hemeldir returned Golodir's reforged sword to you and told you to bring it to Elrond for approval.\n",
[2252]="700301CB\n1\tTalk to Elfsige in Floodwend\tElfsige is in Floodwend, north of the Mead Hall. You have heard that Elfsige has a bow that sounds like it belongs to Corudan, and should ask him to return it.\n2\tTalk to Corudan in Floodwend\tCorudan is in Floodwend, north of the Mead Hall.\n3\tTalk to Alwold outside Floodwend\tAlwold is on the road outside Floodwend. Elfsige has agreed to race you to Elthengels, with the winner of the race taking all claim to Corudan's bow. His commander, Alwold, will start the race.\n",
[2253]="70000190\n1\tBring Golodir's gear to Laerdan\tLaerdan is at Gath Forthnír in the eastern reaches of Himbar. Elrond gave you the sword Dúnachar and told you to take it and the rest of Golodir's gear to Laerdan.\n2\tBring Golodir his equipment\tGolodir is at Gath Forthnír in the eastern reaches of Himbar. Laerdan instructed you to return Golodir's gear to him.\n",
[2254]="700301D4\n1\tTime before Elfsige arrives at Elthengels:\030Reach the entrance to Elthengels before Elfsige does\tElthengels is south-west of Floodwend, and you do not have much time in which to reach it before Elfsige does!\n2\tTalk to Thurhun at the entrance to Elthengels\tYou have arrived at Elthengels, but there is no sign of Elfsige. You should speak with Thurhun, the guard at the entrance to Elthengels, to see if he has seen Elfsige.\n3\tFind Elfsige somewhere between Elthengels and Floodwend\tElfsige may be in trouble among the trees south of the road between Elthengels and Floodwend. Elfsige never arrived at Elthengels, and now you should see if you can find him. He may be in danger!\n4\tTalk to Elfsige in Elthengels\tElfsige has returned to Elthengels, in the Norcrofts. You should return to Elthengels and speak with Elfsige there.\n",
[2255]="700479FD\n1\tTalk to Aragorn at the base of the slag-hill and ride with him to the Black Gate\tAragorn is at the base of the slag-hill outside the Black Gate. Aragorn has asked you to accompany him as he rides to demand the surrender of Sauron, and he wants you to be well-prepared before you go with him.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn on the eastern slag-hill\tAragorn is atop the eastern slag-hill as the Battle of the Black Gate rages outside Mordor. The Mouth of Sauron has revealed that Frodo and Sam have been captured in Mordor. The quest of the Ring has failed.\n",
[2256]="7000019E\n1\tSpeak to Golodir\tMordirith can be found within the throne room of Carn Dûm. Golodir has asked you to join him as he returns to Carn Dûm to face Mordirith, the False King, Steward of Angmar. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Golodir in Gath Forthnír\tGolodir is at Gath Forthnír. After defeating Mordirith and encountering the mysterious Sara Oakheart, you and Golodir travelled back to Gath Forthnír. You should speak with Golodir again.\n",
[2257]="70047A01\n1\tDefeat enemies at the Battle of the Morannon (total: 4)\tOrcs and Uruks have formed a ring around the slag hills, surrounding the Host of the West. Aragorn has asked you to defeat your foes and aid your friends and allies as best you can.\n2\tTalk to Daervunn on the eastern edge of the battle\tDaervunn fights on the south-eastern edge of the eastern slag hill.\n3\tDefeat enemies at the Battle of the Morannon (total: 4)\tOrcs and Uruks have formed a ring around the slag hills, surrounding the Host of the West. Aragorn has asked you to defeat your foes and aid your friends and allies as best you can.\n4\tTalk to Lothrandir on the eastern edge of the battle\tLothrandir is shouting words of support and guidance to the men of the line on the eastern side of the battle.\n5\tDefeat enemies at the Battle of the Morannon (total: 2)\tOrcs and Uruks have formed a ring around the slag hills, surrounding the Host of the West. Aragorn has asked you to defeat your foes and aid your friends and allies as best you can.\n6\tTalk to Gimli on the north-eastern slope of the eastern slag hill\tYou hear the battle-cries of Gimli the Dwarf coming from the north-eastern side of the eastern slag hill.\n7\tTalk to Legolas on the north-eastern slope of the eastern slag hill\tLegolas fights alongside Gimli on the north-eastern side of the eastern slag hill.\n8\tCollect full quivers from the fallen in the ranks of archers (total: 6)\tLines of archers fire into the enemy ranks from their position on the slag hills. Look for full quivers by the bodies of men who have fallen, and gather them for Legolas.\n9\tBring a new supply of full quivers to Legolas on the north-eastern slope of the eastern slag hill\tLegolas fights alongside Gimli on the north-eastern side of the eastern slag hill. You collected a number of full quivers to return to Legolas.\n10\tTalk to Aragorn on top of the eastern slag hill\tAragorn is atop the eastern slag hill.\n11\tFight your way to Prince Imrahil on the south-eastern slope of the western slag hill\tPrince Imrahil is hard-pressed on the slopes of the western slag hill, before the Black Gate. Aragorn has asked you to fight your way across the battlefield to the western slag hill, where you must come to the aid of Prince Imrahil.\n",
[2258]="70030230\n1\tTalk to Horn in Elthengels\tHorn is waiting to speak with you in Elthengels.\n2\tBuy a round of drinks from Thurnoth in the Elthengels tavern\tHorn has given you some coins of the Mark with which to buy a round of drinks for the patrons inside the Elthengels tavern. Perhaps they will have some information to tell you about the Uruks.\n3\tTalk to Wigherd\030Talk to Tidwine\030Talk to Dudmund\tYou have bought a round of drinks with Horn's coins and should now distribute them to the patrons of the Elthengels tavern.\n4\tTalk to Ingild on the first floor of the Elthengels tavern\tA new arrival has come to the Elthengels tavern.\n5\tTalk to Ingild and investigate the sound he heard\tIngild is waiting to talk to you on the first floor of the Elthengels tavern.\n6\tTalk to Thane Mildrith in the Mead Hall of Elthengels\tThane Mildrith is in the mead hall of Elthengels. After the Orc attack, Thane Mildrith has asked you to meet with her.\n",
[2259]="7000019F\n1\tTalk to Aragorn in Rivendell\tAragorn is at Rivendell in the Trollshaws, in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. Golodir instructed you to take word of Mordirith's fall to his chieftain, Aragorn.\n",
[2260]="70047A36\n1\tTalk to Éomer south-east of the western slag hill\tÉomer is south-east of the western slag hill. Prince Imrahil asked you to lend your aid to Éomer of Rohan.\n2\tRohirrim soldiers are being overmatched by their foes to the south-west of Éomer's position at the base of the western slag hill.\t\n3\tDefeat enemies at the Battle of the Morannon (total: 2)\tReeve Ingbert needs time to recover, but he is hard-pressed by his foes!\n4\tProtect Reeve Ingbert while he gets to his feet\tReeve Ingbert is wounded south-east of the base of the western slag hill.\n5\tTalk to Pippin on the southern slope of the western slag hill\030Talk to Beregond on the southern slope of the western slag hill\tPippin and Beregond are halfway up the southern slope of the western slag hill.\n6\tLearn what has so distressed Thalanir on the slope of the western slag hill\tNot far from Pippin and Beregond's location on the western slag hill, a Gondorian soldier calls desperately for your help.\n7\tTalk to Thalanir on the southern slope of the western slag hill\tThalanir is to the west of Pippin and Beregond's location, on the slope of the western slag hill. Something has distressed Thalanir, and the soldier of Gondor calls for your help.\n8\tFind a fallen sword for Thalanir\tThalanir has lost his sword, and the soldier of Gondor has sent you to find a fallen sword on the battlefield to replace the weapon he lost. Fallen swords can be found around the base of the western slag hill near the bodies of their former wielders.\n9\tYou found a sword for Thalanir and should bring it to him on the southern slope of the western slag hill.\t\n10\tYou found a sword for Thalanir and should bring it to him on the southern slope of the western slag hill.\t\n11\tTalk to Éomer atop the western slag hill\tÉomer is on top of the western slag hill.\n12\tDefeat enemies at the Battle of the Morannon (total: 6)\tÉomer has asked you to fight your way back to the eastern slag hill in search of Legolas and Gimli.\n13\tTalk to Legolas on the south-western slope of the eastern slag hill\tLegolas is on the south-western slope of the eastern slag hill.\n14\tDefeat enemies at the Battle of the Morannon (total: 4)\tLegolas has asked you to defeat any enemies you can find as the press of battle surges against the eastern slag hill.\n15\tTalk to Calenglad atop the eastern slag hill\tCalenglad is atop the eastern slag hill.\n16\tTalk to Aragorn atop the eastern slag hill\tAragorn is atop the eastern slag hill.\n",
[2261]="70030233\n1\tTravel to Cliving in the Norcrofts\tCliving is in the Norcrofts, to the north-west of Elthengels. Thane Mildrith of Elthengels is suspicious of Reeve Athelward of Cliving, who took her daughter Siflád as his ward, and wants you to ensure that Siflád is being treated well.\n2\tTalk to Athelward in the Mead Hall of Cliving\tReeve Athelward is in the Mead Hall of Cliving. Thane Mildrith wants you to ensure that her daughter Siflád is not being mistreated. The first step is to introduce yourself to Athelward.\n3\tTalk to Siflád\tSiflád is somewhere in Cliving. Athelward has given you permission to speak to Siflád, his ward.\n4\tTalk to Cuthred in Cliving\tCuthred, the captain of the guard, is by a guard tower in Cliving, west of the Mead Hall. Reeve Athelward wanted you to help the captain of his guard once you had spoken with Siflád.\n",
[2262]="70047A38\n1\tTalk to Aragorn and defy the final enemy assault\tAragorn stands atop the eastern slag hill and prepares to stand against the final enemy attack.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn atop the eastern slag hill\tAragorn is on the eastern slag hill, looking out toward the Black Gate.\n",
[2263]="70030234\n1\tRide to the first marker, east of Cliving\tCuthred has sent you riding the bounds of Cliving: riding east of the city to the first marker, and then turning to your right at each new marker until you have described a great loop around Cliving. He wants you to defeat any mounted enemies you encounter on this circuit as well.\n2\tRide to the second marker, south of the first\tRide to the second marker, south of the first, outside Cliving in the Norcrofts.\n3\tRide to the third marker, west of the second\tRide to the third marker, west of the second, outside Cliving in the Norcrofts.\n4\tRide to the final marker, north of the third one\tRide to the final marker, north of the third, outside Cliving in the Norcrofts.\n5\tTalk to Cuthred in Cliving\tCuthred is in Cliving, near the entrance to the city. You have ridden the bounds, and should now speak to Cuthred, Cliving's captain of the guard.\n",
[2264]="70030232\n1\tTalk to Athelward in the Mead Hall of Cliving\tReeve Athelward is in the Mead Hall of Cliving. Athelward wanted to speak with you and your companions before you depart Cliving.\n2\tTalk to Nona in the Mead Hall of Cliving\030Talk to Horn in the Mead Hall of Cliving\030Talk to Corudan in the Mead Hall of Cliving\tNona, Horn, and Corudan are in the Mead Hall of Cliving with Athelward. You should speak with your companions to determine your next course of action.\n3\tTalk to Athelward in the Mead Hall of Cliving\tReeve Athelward is in the Mead Hall of Cliving. You have spoken with your companions and should now tell Athelward your decision.\n4\tTalk to Thane Mildrith in the Mead Hall of the Elthengels\tThane Mildrith is in the Mead Hall of Elthengels, south-east of Cliving, in the Norcrofts. Reeve Athelward wants you to bring his proposal of marriage to Thane Mildrith.\n",
[2265]="70030312\n1\tCollect Orc Emblems from the Orcs of the Norcrofts (total: 6)\030Scout the river crossing south-west of Elthengels\tThe road runs west of Elthengels for a good way before turning south. At a certain point the southward road crosses the river before it reaches Faldham. Thane Mildrith wants you to travel to Faldham and collect emblems from Orcs in the Norcrofts to show to Elfmar.\n2\tBring the Orc Emblems to Elfmar in the Mead Hall of Faldham\tElfmar is the acting thane of Faldham while his father Elfhelm is away. Thane Mildrith wants you to tell Elfmar of the dangers that face the Norcrofts.\n",
[2266]="70048CDF\n1\tDefeat foes at the Battle of the Morannon (total: 3)\tYou sustained a blow to the head and remember little of the adventures that brought you to this point, but you are in the middle of a battlefield and must fight to survive!\n2\tTalk to Elrohir on the north-west side of the slag-hill\tYou dimly remember Elrohir, one of the sons of Elrond. He stands on the north-west side of the slag-hill and wishes to speak with you.\n3\tTalk to Mithrandir atop the eastern slag-hill during the Battle of the Morannon\tMithrandir stands atop the eastern slag-hill while the Battle of the Morannon rages all about him. Elrohir has seen something on the horizon and has asked you to tell Mithrandir about this new threat.\n",
[2267]="70009E35\n1\tTalk to Golodir\tGolodir is at Gath Forthnír in Angmar, far to the north of Rivendell. Gandalf the Grey has instructed you to return to Gath Forthnír and help Golodir to search for Sara Oakheart and the missing palantír.\n2\tTalk to Sara Oakheart\tSara Oakheart is at Barad Gúlaran in Nan Gurth in Angmar. Barad Gúlaran is located in the centre of a series of bridges that surround it like the spokes of a waggon-wheel. Sara Oakheart was seen by the tower located at the most south-easterly of these bridges. Sara Oakheart has been found outside Barad Gúlaran. Golodir has told you to be careful.\n",
[2268]="70048CEF\n1\tDefeat foes at the Battle of the Morannon (total: 3)\tFoes encircle the Host of the West as the Battle of the Black Gate rages around you.\n2\tTalk to Elrohir\tElrohir stands on the north-west side of the slag-hill and wishes to speak with you.\n3\tTalk to Mithrandir atop the eastern slag-hill during the Battle of the Morannon\tMithrandir stands atop the eastern slag-hill while the Battle of the Morannon rages all about him. Elrohir has seen something on the horizon and has asked you to tell Mithrandir about this new threat.\n",
[2269]="700303B1\n1\tTalk to Éomer outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tÉomer is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Corudan told you that Éomer, the nephew of the King, has returned from his ride north in pursuit of the Uruks.\n2\tTalk to Éothain outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tÉothain is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth, with Éomer. Éomer has told you to ask any questions you have of his man Éothain.\n3\tTalk to Éomer outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tÉomer is outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth. You have spoken with this lieutenant Éothain, and should now speak again with Éomer.\n",
[2270]="70009E36\n1\tHelp Sara Oakheart get to the heart of Barad Gúlaran\tSara Oakheart has asked you to escort her into Barad Gúlaran.\n2\tTalk to Golodir\tGolodir is at Gath Forthnír. You should return to Golodir and tell him what happened at Barad Gúlaran.\n",
[2271]="70048CF0\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir atop the eastern slag-hill and defy the enemy once again\tMithrandir is atop the eastern slag-hill as the Battle of the Morannon rages all around him. The Eagles have flown to the aid of the Host of the West, but will it be enough to turn the tide of battle?\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir on the field of Cormallen\tMithrandir is on the field of Cormallen, waiting to speak with you.\n",
[2272]="700303CE\n1\tFind Éomer's Vengeance, north-west of Eaworth\tÉomer's Vengeance can be found to the north-west of Eaworth, just outside the eaves of Fangorn. Éomer has said you should look for signs of your friends at the site where he encountered and destroyed the Uruks led by Uglúk.\n2\tExamine the remains of Uglúk\tUglúk and Éomer fought personally at the end of the battle, but Uglúk did not walk away.\n3\tThe ground at Éomer's Vengeance is torn up by a confused muddle of footprints. Can anything be learned from it?\t\n4\tTalk to Corudan at Éomer's Vengeance\tCorudan wishes to speak with you at Éomer's Vengeance. You have found a number of footprints that seem to go toward the Forest of Fangorn, and should speak to Corudan about it.\n5\tTalk to Horn at Éomer's Vengeance\tHorn is waiting to speak with you at Éomer's Vengeance, north-west of Eaworth.\n",
})
